I fell directly into **The Drift Friction**. This failure pattern happens when an AI model gradually forgets its initial system persona as a long chat progresses, defaulting back to bland, generic assistant behavior. You end up spending your evening manually editing out buzzwords instead of shipping finished assets.

To maintain perfect alignment across long interactions, you must deploy **Anchor-Locked Custom Instructions**. By embedding imperative behavioral commands directly into your global system settings, you force the engine to filter every output through your core constraints regardless of chat length. Here is the 3-tier system to lock down your assistant's voice:

